index ce0575e..854f549 100644
--- a/.claude/skills/process-email/SKILL.md
+++ b/.claude/skills/process-email/SKILL.md
@@ -91,6 +91,36 @@ A bookmark with no pending mail, missing or merged in full, is
 pointed at the list's tip first. It has nothing to rebase, so the
 rebase alone would leave it behind on an old list.
 
+**Your drafts.** Mail on your bookmark that is not yet in
+`mail@upstream` is a draft, and you may rewrite it until the
+moderator integrates it. Before you pick a message, check each draft
+against what just arrived on trunk and the list:
+
+    jj log -r "mail@upstream..${me}"
+
+- A reply that new mail or trunk has made wrong or incomplete is
+  revised in place: `jj new <commit>`, edit the message file, and
+  `jj squash`. Keep its Message-ID, so it stays one message.
+- A posted series is never revised in place, draft or not. Its
+  version is what review and later versions point at, and a rewrite
+  leaves them pointing at a series nobody can see. If the series
+  needs to change, post the next version (step 5).
+- A draft that is no longer wanted, such as a series for an idea
+  since turned down, is dropped with `jj abandon <commit>`.
+- A draft that is still right is left alone.
+
+The moderator may be reviewing a draft while you revise it, and may
+integrate the original. Once a message is in `mail@upstream` it is
+immutable, so a draft that the rebase above left conflicted with the
+list loses: take the list's version of the file, and abandon the
+draft if that empties it:
+
+    jj restore --from mail@upstream --into <commit> <file>
+
+If the revision still matters, say it in a new reply to the
+integrated message instead. After any change to your drafts, run
+`jj new "${me}"` and `notmuch new` again.
+
 ## 2. Pick the oldest inbox message
 
     id="$(notmuch search --sort=oldest-first --output=messages \
